.TH NUCLEODRIVECTL 1 "" "NucleoDrive" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nucleodrivectl \- control the NucleoDrive background service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nucleodrivectl
.I command
[\fIarguments\fR]
.br
.B nucleodrivectl sync
.I command
[\fIarguments\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Controls the NucleoDrive service, an unofficial Proton Drive client, through its
per-user control socket. When the service is not running, folder and pause
changes are written to its configuration and take effect when it starts.
.SS Backup (one way, local to Drive)
.TP
.B status
Show what the service is doing.
.TP
.B list
List backed-up folders.
.TP
.BI add " local remote"
Back up a local folder to a Drive folder, e.g. ~/Documents /my-files/Documents.
.TP
.BI remove " local"
Stop backing up a folder. Nothing is deleted on Drive.
.TP
.B now
Sync now.
.TP
.B pause
Pause backups.
.TP
.B resume
Resume backups.
.SS Two-way sync
.TP
.B sync status
Show the state of the sync folder (~/proton-drive).
.TP
.B sync list
List the Drive folders that are synced.
.TP
.BI "sync add " folder
Start syncing a Drive folder, given relative to /my-files (e.g. Photos).
.TP
.BI "sync remove " folder
Stop syncing a Drive folder. Nothing is deleted on either side.
.TP
.B sync now
Check Drive for changes now.
.TP
.B sync confirm
Let held-back deletions go through.
.TP
.BR "sync interval " [ when ]
How often Drive is checked: 30, 60, 120 or 240 (minutes), or manual. Without an
argument, show the current setting.
.SH EXIT STATUS
3 if the service is not running (where one is needed).
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/m411s/nucleodrive
